INFO:MLEvolve:Reasoning: The stacking pipeline has a critical inference bug: during training, OOF probabilities for models that failed in some folds are left as all-zeros, and stacker_models is chosen by 'any > 0', but at predict time missing models get uniform 1/n_classes probabilities instead of zeros, so the stacker input distribution differs from training. Additionally, the stacker is fit on OOF predictions from fold-specific vocabularies while base models are refit with full-data vocab, and the fallback path in predict uses a hardcoded uniform fill that silently produces wrong stacker inputs. These cause train/predict skew and degraded accuracy; I will align the predict-time stacker input construction with training (zero-fill for missing models, consistent ordering) and ensure the stacker is only used when all its input models load successfully.
