INFO:MLEvolve:Reasoning: The code has a critical inference bug: LightGBM models are trained with pandas 'category' dtype columns, but at predict time the category dtype is created from the test data's own values, so category codes won't align with training codes, producing garbage predictions. Additionally, CatBoost predict_proba is called on X which still contains the raw string categorical columns (fine for CatBoost), but the LightGBM path needs consistent category mappings persisted from training. I'll fix by persisting per-column category vocabularies and applying them at inference.
