INFO:MLEvolve:Code review for node 4cf611a2fa5744b88415a46b81524f40: needs_revision=True
INFO:MLEvolve:Reasoning: The code has a critical data leakage bug: the stacking meta-learner is trained on OOF predictions from models that were fit on folds, but the OOF predictions for each fold are generated by models trained on the other folds — this is fine. However, the real leakage is that build_features with fit=True is called on the full training features before the CV split, so frequency maps and categorical vocabularies are fit on all training rows including validation folds. Additionally, the stacker is fit on OOF predictions but the base models are then saved and used at inference, while the stacker coefficients were learned from OOF — this is acceptable. The main fix is to fit preprocessing only on training folds, or at minimum acknowledge that frequency encoding on full train data leaks fold information into CV. Also, the stacker is trained on OOF from models that saw the full feature vocab, which is a mild leak. I will restructure to fit preprocessing within each fold.
